e4mc for Horizon — an unofficial port
=====================================

This mod is an UNOFFICIAL port of e4mc to Horizon. It is not made, reviewed,
endorsed or supported by the e4mc project or its authors. Do not report its bugs
to them.

e4mc is a Minecraft mod by vgskye and contributors. This project reimplements,
in Rust for Horizon, what e4mc does for Fabric/NeoForge: ask a relay for a public
domain and forward the players who join it to the local LAN server. No Java code
from e4mc is included here; the game-side code is written against Horizon's own
native hook API, and the relay client is written against the relay's wire
protocol.

Upstream projects this work follows and credits:

  e4mc (Minecraft mod, MIT)
    https://github.com/vgskye/e4mc-minecraft-architectury
    https://modrinth.com/mod/e4mc

  e4mc-quiclime (the relay server, MIT OR Apache-2.0)
    https://github.com/vgskye/e4mc-quiclime

  e4all (a fork of e4mc with an offline-mode option, MIT)
    https://github.com/Synquox/e4all

The relay this mod talks to is run by the e4mc project at e4mc.link. This mod
ships no relay of its own and speaks to no service operated by its author. That
free service has no SLA; `relay_host` in the config points the mod at a
self-hosted e4mc-quiclime instead.

No code from Horizon itself is included here.
